{"crc":"39a31458","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is that `QuerySet.none()` on combined queries (using `union()`) returns all results instead of none. This happens because when a query has a combinator (union, intersection, etc.), the `none()` method doesn't properly handle the combined queries.\n\nThe fix needs to be in `django/db/models/query.py` in the `none()` method. When a query has a combinator, we need to apply `none()` to each of the combined queries.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/models/query.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def none(self):\n        \"\"\"Return an empty QuerySet.\"\"\"\n        clone = self._chain()\n        if clone.query.combinator:\n            clone.query.combined_queries = tuple(\n                query.clone() for query in clone.query.combined_queries\n            )\n            for query in clone.query.combined_queries:\n                query.set_empty()\n        else:\n            clone.query.set_empty()\n        return clone\n=======\n    def none(self):\n        \"\"\"Return an empty QuerySet.\"\"\"\n        clone = self._chain()\n        if clone.query.combinator:\n            clone.query.combined_queries = tuple(\n                query.none() for query in clone.query.combined_queries\n            )\n        else:\n            clone.query.set_empty()\n        return clone\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQAMK39B2233T0V3AE4RAT0","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQAMK339Y26HYYZZAH11F44"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786415568.38138}
